# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Provider credentials -------------------------------------------------
# litellm reads this directly. DESIGN.md Appendix routes extractor and judge
# through litellm so a model swap is a config line, not a code change.
#
# Only the EXTRACTOR needs this now (see the role block below). Do not export it
# by hand with `$env:GROQ_API_KEY="gsk_..."`: PowerShell writes that line to
# ConsoleHost_history.txt, and a process-environment value silently WINS over
# this file, so a rotated key here can sit shadowed by a revoked one.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- The three LLM roles (DESIGN.md 2, "Why three distinct LLM roles") -----
# Temperatures are prescribed by the design and should not be "tuned":
#   extractor 0.0  - read literally, refuse to infer
#   adversary 0.9  - write the most tempting phrasing a real customer would use
#   judge     0.0  - decide what the response committed to, cite the clause
#
# IMPORTANT (DESIGN.md 1.5): the judge must come from a DIFFERENT MODEL FAMILY
# than the agent under test. The agent runs Qwen (qwen2.5:7b-instruct), frozen in
# its own code. If you change any model below, re-check the families or the
# separation is lost silently - `tests/unit/test_aut_contract.py` asserts it, and
# `tests/model_families.py` is the one place the comparison is implemented.
#
# Re-pinned 2026-08-23: the previous judge and extractor model,
# groq/llama-3.3-70b-versatile, was decommissioned by the provider and started
# returning 404 model_not_found. DESIGN.md names no model ID except the agent's
# Qwen, because an ID is provider inventory and a family is a property of the
# measurement. The four roles are now four DISTINCT families - agent qwen,
# extractor gpt, judge llama, adversary mistral - where before the judge and the
# adversary were both Llama and differed only in size. DESIGN.md 2 warns that
# "a model that generated a probe is measurably more likely to accept a response
# that pattern-matches its own generation", so that is a real improvement.
#
# Judge and adversary are LOCAL. Pull them once, or the live tests skip:
#   ollama pull llama3.1:8b
#   ollama pull mistral:7b
CLAUSEGUARD_EXTRACTOR_MODEL=groq/openai/gpt-oss-120b
CLAUSEGUARD_EXTRACTOR_TEMP=0.0

CLAUSEGUARD_ADVERSARY_MODEL=ollama_chat/mistral:7b
CLAUSEGUARD_ADVERSARY_TEMP=0.9

CLAUSEGUARD_JUDGE_MODEL=ollama_chat/llama3.1:8b
CLAUSEGUARD_JUDGE_TEMP=0.0
# k=3 majority vote is applied ONLY to over-promise judgments and the gold set
# (DESIGN.md 4.1 L3 - "take the asymmetry").
CLAUSEGUARD_JUDGE_CONSISTENCY_K=3
CLAUSEGUARD_JUDGE_CONSISTENCY_TEMP=0.3

# Where the HARNESS's own litellm calls reach Ollama. Read by litellm, not by us.
# This is the third similarly-named setting in this file and they are all
# different things, so: OLLAMA_API_BASE is the harness talking to Ollama from the
# host; AUT_OLLAMA_HOST below is the agent talking to Ollama from inside its
# container; OLLAMA_HOST is Ollama's own SERVER BIND address and is not set here
# at all. Leave this commented out unless Ollama is not on the default port -
# litellm already defaults to http://localhost:11434.
# OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434

# --- Agents under test ----------------------------------------------------
# The harness talks to both over HTTP only. No shared imports (DESIGN.md 1.4).
AUT_NAIVE_URL=http://localhost:8001
AUT_STRONG_URL=http://localhost:8002

# aut-naive backend switch. "ollama" is the documented default per DESIGN.md
# 1.4; "groq" exists so the agent can run where Ollama cannot.
# Note the family constraint above: the groq fallback is deliberately a Qwen
# model so the Llama judge stays in a different family either way.
#
# These names are what the agent's backends.py actually reads. AUT_OLLAMA_HOST is
# deliberately NOT called OLLAMA_HOST: Ollama itself reads OLLAMA_HOST to choose
# its server bind address (set it to 0.0.0.0:11434 on the host so the container
# can reach it), and that value is useless as a client target.
LLM_BACKEND=ollama
AUT_OLLAMA_HOST=http://host.docker.internal:11434
# The fallback's compiled-in default (qwen/qwen3-32b) was decommissioned in the
# same 2026-08-23 sweep, but it lives inside the frozen tree and CANNOT be edited:
# the aut-naive-v1 tag records `git rev-parse HEAD:aut-naive`, and moving a tag
# would make every audit row that cites it unverifiable (commitment C3). So the
# revival happens here instead - backends.py reads GROQ_MODEL ahead of its own
# constant. It must stay a QWEN model, which is what the family test enforces.
GROQ_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.6-27b
# Frozen in code, not configurable: model qwen2.5:7b-instruct, temperature 0.7,
# top-k 3. A frozen agent whose behaviour moves with an env var is not frozen
# (commitment C3), so these live as constants in backends.py / prompts.py /
# retrieval.py and are reported at /health rather than being read from here.

# --- Execution ------------------------------------------------------------
# Semaphore of 8 for the async httpx fan-out (DESIGN.md 2 step 6).
CLAUSEGUARD_CONCURRENCY=8
CLAUSEGUARD_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_S=120

# --- Audit store ----------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite, append-only, downloadable by a panelist (DESIGN.md 1.6).
CLAUSEGUARD_DB_PATH=runs.db
